andle carrying over:\n\n1. **Identify the place value**: Start by identifying the place value where the sum of digits is 10 or more. This could be the units place, tens place, hundreds place, and so on.\n\n2. **Add the digits**: Add the digits in the identified place value.\n\n3. **Determine the carry-over**: If the sum is 10 or more, write down the units digit of the sum in the current place value and carry over the tens digit to the next higher place value.\n\n4. **Move to the next place value**: Move to the next higher place value and repeat the process. If there is a carry-over from the previous place value, add it to the sum of the digits in the current place value.\n\n5. **Continue the process**: Continue this process for all place values until you have added all the digits.\n\nLet's illustrate this with an example using the numbers 758871560 and 047067498:\n\n1. **Units place**: \n   - 7 (from 758871560) + 2 (from 047067498) = 9\n   - Write down 9 and move to the next place value.\n\n2. **Tens place**: \n   - 1 (from 758871560) + 3 (from 047067498) = 4\n   - Write down 4 and move to the next place value.\n\n3. **Hundreds place**: \n   - 0 (from 758871560) + 4 (from 047067498) = 4\n   - Write down 4 and move to the next place value.\n\n4. **Thousands place**: \n   - 5 (from 758871560) + 5 (from 047067498) = 10\n   - Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \n   - 9 (from 758871560) + 9 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 19\n   - Write down 9 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \n   - 5 (from 758871560) + 5 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n7. **Millions place**: \n   - 8 (from 758871560) + 8 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 17\n   - Write down 7 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n8. **Ten millions place**: \n   - 4 (from 758871560) + 7 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 12\n   - Write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n9. **Hundred millions place**: \n   - 2 (from 758871560) + 7 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 10\n   - Write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next place value.\n\n10. **Billion place**: \n    - 0 (from 758871560) + 0 (from 047067498) + 1 (carry-over) = 1\n    - Write down 1.\n\nBy following these steps, we can handle carrying over when the sum of digits in a place value is 10 or more, ensuring that we correctly add the numbers and arrive at the final sum. In the example given, the final sum is 205844853. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! When the sum of digits in a place value is 10 or more, we handle the carrying over by writing down the units digit of the sum in the current place value and carrying over the tens digit to the next higher place value. Here's a step-by-step explanation:\n\n1. **Identify the place value**: Start by identifying the place value where the sum of digits is 10 or more. This could be the units place, tens place, hundreds place, and so on.\n\n2. **Add the digits**: Add the digits in the identified place value.\n\n3. **Determine the carry-over**: If the sum is 10 or more, write down the units digit of the sum in the current place value and carry over the tens digit to the next higher place value.\n\n4. **Move to the next place value**: Move to the next higher place value and repeat the process. If there is a carry-over from the previous place value, add it to the sum of the digits in the current place value.\n\n5. **Continue the process**: Continue this process for all place values until you have added all the digits.\n\nLet's illustrate this with the numbers 758871560 and 047067498:\n\n1. **Units place**: \n   - 7 (from 758871560) + 2 (from 047067498) = 9\n   - Write down 9 and move to the next place value.\n\n2. **Tens place**: \n   - 1 (from 758871560) + 3 (from 047067498) = 4\n   - Write down 4 and move to the next place value.\n\n3. **Hundreds place**: \n   - 0 (from 758871560) + 4 (from 04706