ertainly! Handling carrying over when the sum of digits in a place value is 10 or more, especially when there are multiple carry-overs, involves a step-by-step process of adding the digits and carrying over appropriately. Here's a detailed explanation:\n\n1. **Identify the place value**: Start by identifying the place value where the sum of digits is 10 or more. This could be the units place, tens place, hundreds place, and so on.\n\n2. **Add the digits**: Add the digits in the identified place value.\n\n3. **Determine the carry-over**: If the sum is 10 or more, write down the units digit of the sum in the current place value and carry over the tens digit to the next higher place value.\n\n4. **Move to the next place value**: Move to the next higher place value and repeat the process. If there is a carry-over from the previous place value, add it to the sum of the digits in the current place value.\n\n5. **Continue the process**: Continue this process for all place values until you have added all the digits.\n\nLet's illustrate this with an example where there are multiple carry-overs:\n\nConsider the addition of 123456789 and 987654321:\n\n```\n  123456789\n+ 987654321\n---------\n```\n\n1. **Units place**: \n   - 9 (from 123456789) + 1 (from 987654321) = 10\n   - Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\n2. **Tens place**: \n   - 8 (from 123456789) + 2 (from 987654321) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n3. **Hundreds place**: \n   - 7 (from 123456789) + 3 (from 987654321) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n4. **Thousands place**: \n   - 6 (from 123456789) + 4 (from 987654321) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \n   - 5 (from 123456789) + 5 (from 987654321) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \n   - 4 (from 123456789) + 6 (from 987654321) + 1 (carry-over) = 11\n   - Write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\n7. **Mill