 ```\n     11)1234\n     11\n   ------\n      24\n   ```\n\n8. **Divide the new number**: 24 \u00f7 11.\n   - 24 \u00f7 11 = 2 (since 11 x 2 = 22, which is the largest multiple of 11 that is less than or equal to 24).\n   - Write 2 above the division bar, above the 4.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     112\n   ```\n\n9. **Subtract**: Subtract 22 from 24.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     112\n   ------\n      12\n   ```\n\n10. **Final result**: Since 12 is less than 11, we stop here. The quotient is 112 and the remainder is 12.\n    ```\n     11)1234\n     112\n   ------\n      12\n   ```\n\nTherefore, the result of 1234 \u00f7 11 is 112 with a remainder of 12.\n\nLet's verify this step-by-step solution:\n```\n     11)1234\n     112\n   ------\n      12\n```\n\nBy following these steps, you can solve division problems systematically. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Let's solve the division problem of 1234 \u00f7 11 step by step:\n\n1. **Setup the division**: Write 1234 under the division bar and 11 outside.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n   ```\n\n2. **Divide the first digit**: 12 (the first two digits of 1234) by 11.\n   - 12 \u00f7 11 = 1 (since 11 x 1 = 11, which is the largest multiple of 11 that is less than or equal to 12).\n   - Write 1 above the division bar, above the 2.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     1\n   ```\n\n3. **Subtract**: Subtract 11 from 12.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     1\n   ------\n      1\n   ```\n\n4. **Bring down the next digit**: Bring down the 3 to make it 13.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     1\n   ------\n      13\n   ```\n\n5. **Divide the new number**: 13 \u00f7 11.\n   - 13 \u00f7 11 = 1 (since 11 x 1 = 11, which is the largest multiple of 11 that is less than or equal to 13).\n   - Write 1 above the division bar, above the 3.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     11\n   ```\n\n6. **Subtract**: Subtract 11 from 13.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     11\n   ------\n      2\n   ```\n\n7. **Bring down the next digit**: Bring down the 4 to make it 24.\n   ```\n     11)1234\n     11\n 